# ROOT Website Rules

## Mission
- Every public-site change must improve sales conversion, credibility, accessibility, discoverability, or reliability.
- Primary conversion: the fixed-fee $2,500 Revenue Optimization Diagnostic.
- ROOT is the parent commercial/MSO brand. DIRT is the Data Intelligence for Revenue Transformation capability inside ROOT.

## Architecture
- Preserve React + Vite + GitHub Pages unless a proven operating constraint requires change.
- Preserve the existing Clinical Glass CSS system. Do not activate Tailwind or perform a CSS-framework migration without an explicit architecture decision.
- Prefer existing components, `src/siteData.js`, proof data, and DIRT-derived command-view patterns before creating replacements.
- Keep content/data separate from reusable UI wherever practical.

## Visual system
- Premium US healthcare operations: clinical, analytical, executive, calm, precise.
- Avoid generic smiling-doctor, hospital-corridor, call-center, crypto/neon, or decorative stock imagery.
- DIRT visual language may contribute indigo/aqua/emerald command-center signals inside ROOT analytical surfaces.
- Never fabricate client dashboards, testimonials, logos, outcomes, certifications, payer relationships, or performance guarantees.
- Prevent CLS: reserve media dimensions/aspect ratios and lazy-load below-fold media.

## Conversion and experiments
- Preserve CTA data attributes and deidentified experiment attribution.
- Experiments must be persistent, testable, reversible, and must not change pricing or unsupported claims.
- Never put form contents or PHI into analytics/CTA events.

## Forms and privacy
- Public forms are commercial/no-PHI only and must keep the mandatory no-PHI acknowledgement.
- Production inquiries must deliver to `info@rootrcm.com`; phone is `+1 (302) 506 4685`; WhatsApp is `https://wa.me/13025064685`.
- Do not add PHI storage, public file uploads, secrets, credentials, or patient data.

## SEO and accessibility
- One meaningful H1 per page; preserve semantic heading order.
- Maintain page-specific title, description, canonical, Open Graph, Twitter metadata, structured data, sitemap, and robots behavior.
- Utility/success pages must not be indexed.
- Interactive navigation must work by keyboard, expose state with ARIA, support Escape, and preserve visible focus.
- Decorative imagery uses empty alt text; informative imagery uses concise contextual alt text.

## Quality gate
Before merge run: `npm ci`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`.
Do not merge a failing head.
